# Code owners for the community-health files under templates/.
#
# These files are copied into each repo by `scripts/onboard.py` (and kept
# current by `scripts/sync.py`) -- not served by GitHub's community-health
# inheritance, which only reaches into a `.github` repo automatically. A
# change here doesn't reach a repo that already onboarded until that repo
# syncs again, so getting the wording right before it goes out is what
# "owned rather than open" buys.
#
# CODEOWNERS itself was never one of the files GitHub's inheritance would
# have served anyway -- that has nothing to do with copy vs. inheritance.

